          "title": "Bound each actual diagonal value",
          "text": "Since κ≥2, its cosine coefficient is nonnegative. Multiply the standard bounds −1≤cos θᵢ≤1 by that coefficient to obtain the exact source interval, without a spectral-window premise.",
          "formula": "\\begin{aligned}\\lambda_i-1&=\\tfrac{\\kappa-1}{2}(1+\\cos\\theta_i)\\ge0,\\\\\\kappa-\\lambda_i&=\\tfrac{\\kappa-1}{2}(1-\\cos\\theta_i)\\ge0.\\end{aligned}",
          "lean": "hcoef is derived from hκ; hvalue consumes Real.neg_one_le_cos, Real.cos_le_one and exact real arithmetic."
        },
        {
          "title": "Form the two positive diagonal differences",
          "text": "Use the actual scalar differences as diagonal entries. Nonnegative diagonal entries make these two actual diagonal matrices positive semidefinite, including their symmetry.",
          "formula": "D_-=\\operatorname{diag}(\\lambda_i-1)\\succeq0,\\qquad D_+=\\operatorname{diag}(\\kappa-\\lambda_i)\\succeq0.",
          "lean": "hdiaglo/hdiaghi prove the actual matrix identities entrywise; hlow/hhigh call the canonical PosSemidef.diagonal fact on the proved scalar bounds."
        },
        {
          "title": "Conjugate through the actual rotation",
          "text": "Use OOᵀ=I from full real orthogonality. Distributing the actual products identifies the two differences with conjugates of the proved positive diagonal matrices. Positive semidefiniteness is preserved under this actual conjugation.",
          "formula": "\\begin{aligned}A-I_d&=O D_-O^\\top\\succeq0,\\\\\\kappa I_d-A&=O D_+O^\\top\\succeq0.\\end{aligned}",
          "lean": "hO, hstar and the distribution identities hloweq/hhigheq feed hAlo/hAhi via PosSemidef.mul_mul_conjTranspose_same."
        },
        {
          "title": "Produce strict positivity",
          "text": "Add the positive identity matrix to the first semidefinite difference. Every nonzero vector has strictly positive identity quadratic form, so the actual precision is positive definite. This is an output consequence.",
          "formula": "x\\ne0\\ \\Longrightarrow\\ x^\\top A x=\\|x\\|_2^2+x^\\top(A-I_d)x>0.",
          "lean": "hpos combines the canonical PosDef.one and PosDef.posSemidef_add with hAlo, then cancels the subtracted identity."
        },
        {
          "title": "Consume the actual precision in its Gaussian density",
          "text": "The focused Test applies the producer to this same literal A and passes its positive-definite output to the existing canonical positive-precision Gaussian density theorem. The actual inverse-covariance Gaussian equals the actual quadratic-potential density, with no supplied positivity or correct-density hypothesis.",
